{
  "description": "This page serves as a technical playground for testing UI components and utility hooks within the creator dashboard. Creators use these components to manage goods packs and perform administrative actions. The interface demonstrates common button variants and provides a real-time display of the current responsive screen breakpoint. The translation keys \"Active range\" and \"Active range2\" act as labels for the detected device screen size. Please ensure these labels are concise to fit within the responsive debugging display. Note that the \"Active range2\" string appears to be a redundant placeholder for this demonstration; translate it according to its label context.",
  "sourceSnapshot": "<script lang=\"ts\" setup>\n  const screen = useScreen()\n  const clicks = ref(0)\n  const screenReady = ref(false)\n\n  const activeScreen = computed(() => {\n    const screens = ['base', 'sm', 'md', 'lg', 'xl', 'xxl'] as const\n\n    return screens.find((key) => screen[key]) ?? 'unknown'\n  })\n  const { theme } = useTheme()\n\n  onMounted(async () => {\n    await screen.ready\n    screenReady.value = true\n  })\n</script>\n\n<template>\n  <main class=\"mx-auto max-w-3xl space-y-10 p-6 sm:p-10\">\n    <section class=\"space-y-4 text-alt-400 hover:bg-alt-950\">\n      <p class=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-500\">BrickButton</p>\n      <div class=\"flex flex-wrap items-center gap-3\">\n        <BrickButton @click=\"clicks += 1\">\n          <template #leading><span aria-hidden=\"true\">+</span></template>\n          Add item\n        </BrickButton>\n        <BrickButton\n          color=\"plain\"\n          variant=\"solid\"\n        >\n          Secondary\n        </BrickButton>\n        <BrickButton\n          color=\"win\"\n          variant=\"soft\"\n          to=\"/demo\"\n        >\n          Link demo\n        </BrickButton>\n        <BrickButton\n          color=\"danger\"\n          variant=\"ghost\"\n          square\n          aria-label=\"Delete\"\n        >\n          ×\n        </BrickButton>\n        <BrickButton\n          color=\"alt\"\n          variant=\"ghost\"\n        >\n          Clicked {{ clicks }} times\n        </BrickButton>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n\n    <ClientOnly>{{ theme }}</ClientOnly>\n    <section class=\"space-y-4\">\n      <p class=\"text-sm font-medium text-gray-500\">useScreen</p>\n      <p class=\"text-sm text-gray-300\">\n        <template v-if=\"screenReady\">\n          {{ t('Active range') }}: {{ t('Active range2') }}:\n          <strong>{{ activeScreen }}</strong>\n        </template>\n        <template v-else>Detecting screen size…</template>\n      </p>\n      <div class=\"grid gap-2 rounded-lg bg-gray-100 p-3 text-sm font-medium text-gray-700\">\n        <p :class=\"screen.baseClass\">base: under 40rem</p>\n        <p :class=\"screen.smClass\">sm: 40rem–48rem</p>\n        <p :class=\"screen.mdClass\">md: 48rem–64rem</p>\n        <p :class=\"screen.lgClass\">lg: 64rem–80rem</p>\n        <p :class=\"screen.xlClass\">xl: 80rem–96rem</p>\n        <p :class=\"screen.xxlClass\">xxl: 96rem and up</p>\n      </div>\n    </section>\n  </main>\n</template>\n"
}
